  "_comment_pool": "2 = System. Measured 2026-07-29, three ways, all identical at ~6 MiB of heap: pool_partition 1 (Applet) alone, a 128 MiB pm:shell boost alone, and both together. The ceiling is Atmosphere's: it already steals from the applet pool for the system pool, and firmware 20.0.0 capped that steal at 14 MB for every custom sysmodule on the console combined. There is no configuration for it (Atmosphere PR #697, rejected: pm runs before set:sys). The way around it is not this pool at all but the 'memlet' service below, which hands out APPLET-pool memory charged to someone else's limit.",
